$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure I (for cat.1, cat .3 and cat.5) N-Boc-amino acid (10
mmol) was dissolved in THF (25 mL) and cooled in an ice bath. NMM (10
mmol) and ethyl chloroformate ( 10 mmol) were added to the aboved cooled
solution and stirred for 30min. The resulting mixture was treated with
sulfonyl hydrazide (1.2 eq, 12mmol) at 0 °C. After 2h the solvent THF was
evaporated and the residue was dissolved in DCM (200 mL). Then the DCM
layer was washed with hydrogen chloride solution (2M, 60×3 mL) and brine
subsequently. The solvent was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and evaporated
in vacuum. The crude product which could be used in next step directly.
The above crude product was dissolved in DCM (50 mL) and cooled in an ice
bath. TFA (100 mmol) was added and stirred overnight. The resulting
mixture was evaporated in vacuum and the residue was dissolved in DCM
(100 mL). Then the DCM layer was washed with Na2CO3 saturated solution
(30×3 mL) and a lot of precipitate appeared in the cases of cat.1 and
cat.3. The precipitate was filtered and washed with water and ice-cooled
ethanol subsequently. The obtained solid was dried in vacuum furthermore
and the obtained product could be used in reaction as catalyst directly.
In the case of cat.5, the DCM layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and
removed in vacuum. The crude product was further purified by flash
chromatography ( DCM/Methanol = 20/1 ).
(S)-N'-(2-amino-3-phenylpropanoyl)-2-nitrobenzenesulfonohy drazide
(cat.1): white solid in 92 % yield. M.p. 96-100 °C. [α]D 20 +2.6 (c =
1.0, THF); 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.11-8.04 (m,2H), 7.80-7.73 (m, 2H),
7.32-7.26 (m, 3H), 7.11-7.09 (m, 2H), 3.55-3.52 (dd, J = 4.0 Hz, J = 9.6
Hz, 1H) 3.00-2.96 (dd, J = 4.0 Hz, J = 13.6 Hz, 1H), 2.54-2.48 (dd, J =
9.6 Hz, J = 13.6 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 172.94, 147.80,
136.62, 134.50, 132.76, 132.49, 131.63, 129.11, 128.89, 127.19, 126.22,
55.52, 40.41; IR (film, ν/cm-1 ): 3253, 3093, 3026, 2926, 1688, 1539,
1356, 1277, 1356, 1175, 1126, 854, 739; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C15H16N4O5S [M+H]+ 365.0920, found 365.0917.
